1. System Information & Hardware Checks
View Windows version and system details
# systeminfo

Check running processes
#tasklist

End a stuck program
#taskkill /IM programname.exe /F

Example:
#taskkill /IM chrome.exe /F

Open Task Manager
#taskmgr



2. System File Repair Commands
Check and repair corrupted Windows system files
#sfc /scannow

Repair Windows component store
#DISM /Online /Cleanup-Image /RestoreHealth

Recommended order:
#DISM /Online /Cleanup-Image /RestoreHealth
#sfc /scannow



3. Disk Troubleshooting
Check disk errors
#chkdsk

Scan and repair disk errors
#chkdsk C: /f /r
(Requires restart if the drive is in use.)

Check disk space
#wmic logicaldisk get size,freespace,caption



4. Network Troubleshooting
View IP address
#ipconfig

Detailed network information
#ipconfig /all

Release and renew IP address
#ipconfig /release
#ipconfig /renew

Clear DNS cache
#ipconfig /flushdns

Test internet connectivity
#ping google.com

Check network route
#tracert google.com

View saved Wi-Fi profiles
#netsh wlan show profiles

Reset network settings
#netsh winsock reset



5. Windows Services Troubleshooting
Open Services
#services.msc

Check running services
#net start

Restart a service
#net stop servicename
#net start servicename

Example:
#net stop spooler
#net start spooler



6. Startup & Boot Repair
Open System Configuration
#msconfig

Check boot configuration
#bcdedit

Repair boot records (from Recovery Environment)
#bootrec /fixmbr
#bootrec /fixboot
#bootrec /rebuildbcd



7. User Account Troubleshooting
View users
#net user

Create a local user
#net user username password /add

View administrator accounts
#net localgroup administrators



8. Event Logs & Diagnostics
Open Event Viewer
#eventvwr.msc

Open Reliability Monitor
#perfmon /rel

Open Performance Monitor
#perfmon



9. Remote & Network Administration
Check hostname
#hostname

Check active connections
#netstat -ano

Find a process using a port
#netstat -ano | findstr :8080



