1.Open PowerShell as Administrator:
#Install the Windows Update module:
#Install-Module PSWindowsUpdate

Import the module:
#Import-Module PSWindowsUpdate

Check available updates:
#Get-WindowsUpdate

Install all available updates:
#Install-WindowsUpdate -AcceptAll -AutoReboot



2. Using Windows Update service commands (CMD)
Restart Windows Update services:
#net stop wuauserv
#net stop bits
#net start bits
#net start wuauserv



3. Force Windows Update Check
#usoclient StartScan

Start downloading updates:
#usoclient StartDownload

Install updates:
#usoclient StartInstall

Restart after updates:
#shutdown /r /t 0



4. Repair Windows Update Components
If Windows Update is stuck:

#net stop wuauserv
#net stop bits
#net stop cryptsvc
#net stop msiserver

Rename update cache folders:
#ren C:\Windows\SoftwareDistribution SoftwareDistribution.old
#ren C:\Windows\System32\catroot2 catroot2.old

Start services again:
#net start wuauserv
#net start bits
#net start cryptsvc
#net start msiserver



5. Check Windows Update Status
#Get-Service wuauserv

View installed updates:
#wmic qfe list

